WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.738
An AI hallucination isn't a glitch. It's the model doing exactly what it was built to do — produce a fluent, confident answer, whether or not it happens to be true.

00:09.738 --> 00:19.154
You can't delete them. You can catch them. Ground the model in real sources, then check every answer against those sources — does the claim actually appear in the data?

00:19.154 --> 00:30.707
The dangerous ones are confident and specific: a fake policy, a wrong number, a made-up citation. So I test for exactly those, on real inputs, and flag them before they reach a user.

00:30.707 --> 00:35.387
The goal isn't zero hallucinations. It's zero that ever reach your customer.

00:35.387 --> 00:38.341
Catch them before they cost you. Let's talk.

